## Member project: read this first

- **Not self-governed.** This project has no `.agents/config.yaml`, on purpose: the company's rules and guards stay in force here. Where the text below says `scope: project`, or points into `.agents/` (`project-init.md`, memory, docs, `CAPABILITIES.md`, hooks, skills) or at `just`, it describes a yard-scaffolded project and does not apply to this one.
- **The standard** — [docs/project-standard.md](docs/project-standard.md): the naming standard, the language by layer, the tests layout, the memory route, and where each laid-down file comes from.
- **Tests** — `sh tests/run.sh` runs every suite in `tests/suites.txt` and ends with one `<project>: N passed, M failed` line. One suite per unit (`tests/<unit>/<unit>.test.sh`), red first: write the test, watch it fail, then write the code. `tests/example/example.test.sh` shows the shape.
